-- Type-directed name resolution through a SECTION binder.
--
-- `ok/tdnr.l4` pins the same property for module-level ASSUMEs: one name may be
-- bound several times at different types, and each occurrence resolves by the
-- type its context demands. A section GIVEN is ruled (R3/R4) to resolve exactly
-- as a same-section ASSUME does, so the same file written with the binder on
-- the heading must behave identically -- including through the printer, which
-- re-emits the GivenSig rather than the elaborations it desugars to.

§ `Type-directed name resolution through a section binder`
    GIVEN foo IS A NUMBER
          foo IS A BOOLEAN
          foo IS A STRING

DECIDE bar
  IS foo + 2

DECIDE baz
  IS NOT foo

DECIDE all
  IS IF foo THEN foo ELSE "foo"
